{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"The target proposes a substantive reduction relation ('intentional inefficiency reduces to operational heterogeneity as stochastic filters') and names a refuter ('standardized best-practice configuration proving equal or greater isolation'). However, it asserts a causal mechanism without providing any evidence or distinguishing test for the core problem's demand: what evidence would separate truly independent failures from merely-uncorrelated-until-shared-cause failures. Stochastic filtering via idiosyncratic configurations could itself mask a shared root cause (e.g., a common hardware vendor vulnerability that manifests stochastically across heterogeneous setups), making failures appear independent when they are not. The refutation condition only tests whether standardization beats heterogeneity on isolation, but never addresses whether heterogeneity genuinely produces independent failures or merely defers the discovery of correlation. This leaves the central evidentiary question of the problem unanswered.","target":"afb6effcb0eaf31469eb6fdd0ce8266b82cf5d909d87ea0b217d2c3c69125558"},{"attack":true,"case":"The mechanism asserted—heterogeneity avoiding monoculture and capping infection rates below 100%—does not establish that decentralized failures are causally independent rather than merely appearing uncorrelated. The biological-style mutation shield analogy is offered as mechanism but no evidence-generating test is proposed to distinguish true independence from latent shared causes. The countercondition (hyper-standardization) identifies a risk but does not supply the distinguishing evidence the problem explicitly demands. The mechanism also conflates exploit-propagation resistance with correlated-failure independence: heterogeneous configurations may all share a hidden dependency (e.g., a common upstream library or certificate authority) that produces correlated failures invisible until triggered, which the mutation-shield framing cannot detect or rule out.","target":"fa12bf00a4c9f4713f1d53580fea85b97b95cc57862531d1cf9e102401fe8b32"}]}